+## 14. RVFI Trace File Output (`--rvfi-output`)
+
+When running in instruction-file mode (`-f`), the simulator can write a
+binary RVFI V1 trace to a file in addition to the ELF memory dump.  This
+lets you capture the complete cycle-accurate execution record and compare it
+offline against an RTL simulation.
+
+### How it works
+
+The RVFI trace format is the same binary wire format used by socket mode
+(RVFI V1, 88 bytes per packet, little-endian).  After every `zstep()` call
+the simulator calls `rvfi_send_trace()`, which writes one execution packet to
+the trace file.  At the end of the instruction sequence a **halt packet** is
+appended so that the file is self-contained and can be compared directly with
+RTL traces that use the same convention.
+
+### Flags
+
+| Flag | Description |
+|---|---|
+| `--rvfi-output <path>` | Write binary RVFI V1 packets to `<path>`. Optional. If omitted, no trace file is produced. |
+| `--elf-output <path>` | Write the post-execution ELF memory dump to `<path>` instead of the auto-generated `memdump_XXXXXX.elf` name. Optional. |
+
+### Example
+
+```bash
+# Run instruction file, capturing RVFI trace and ELF dump
+./c_emulator/cheri_riscv_rvfi_RV32 \
+    --instr-file   dii_inputs/test_01.txt \
+    --rvfi-output  dii_outputs/test_01/rvfi.bin \
+    --elf-output   dii_outputs/test_01/run.elf
+```
+
+After this command:
+- `dii_outputs/test_01/rvfi.bin` — binary RVFI trace (one 88-byte packet per instruction + one halt packet)
+- `dii_outputs/test_01/run.elf` — post-execution ELF for re-execution or inspection
+
+---
+
+## 15. Batch Mode
+
+The `scripts/batch_run.sh` script automates running many instruction files
+through the simulator and collecting the outputs.
+
+### Directory layout expected
+
+```
+dii_inputs/
+    test_01.txt
+    test_02.txt
+    ...
+```
+
+### Running the batch
+
+```bash
+# Default: simulator at ./c_emulator/cheri_riscv_rvfi_RV32,
+#          inputs from ./dii_inputs, outputs to ./dii_outputs
+./scripts/batch_run.sh
+
+# Specify paths explicitly
+./scripts/batch_run.sh \
+    --sim       ./c_emulator/cheri_riscv_rvfi_RV32 \
+    --instr-dir ./dii_inputs \
+    --output-dir ./dii_outputs
+
+# Parallel execution (requires GNU parallel)
+./scripts/batch_run.sh --jobs 8
+```
+
+### Output layout
+
+For each `dii_inputs/<stem>.txt` the script produces:
+
+```
+dii_outputs/
+    <stem>/
+        run.elf     — post-execution ELF memory dump
+        rvfi.bin    — binary RVFI trace (88 bytes/packet)
+        sim.log     — simulator stderr log
+```
+
+### Generating instruction files
+
+The simulator expects plain-text instruction files — one 32-bit hexadecimal
+instruction word per line.  These can be generated by any RTL test-vector
+tool, by hand, or by a script.  Example with a simple Python generator:
+
+```python
+# gen_dii.py — write 100 random NOP sequences
+import random, pathlib
+pathlib.Path("dii_inputs").mkdir(exist_ok=True)
+for i in range(100):
+    with open(f"dii_inputs/test_{i:03d}.txt", "w") as f:
+        for _ in range(random.randint(5, 20)):
+            f.write("00000013\n")  # NOP (ADDI x0, x0, 0)
+```
+
+---
+
+## 16. Comparing Sail vs RTL Traces
+
+`scripts/compare_rvfi.py` parses binary RVFI V1 trace files and compares
+them field-by-field.
+
+### Single-pair comparison
+
+```bash
+python3 scripts/compare_rvfi.py \
+    --sail dii_outputs/test_01/rvfi.bin \
+    --rtl  rtl_outputs/test_01/rvfi.bin
+```
+
+Sample output on mismatch:
+
+```
+  [test_01] FAIL — 2 mismatch(es)  (sail=15 pkts, rtl=15 pkts)
+
+  Packet #3:
+    rd_wdata            sail=0x0000000000000000  rtl=0x0000000000000005
+
+  Packet #7:
+    pc_wdata            sail=0x0000000080000014  rtl=0x0000000080000018
+```
+
+### Directory-pair comparison
+
+```bash
+# Compare all tests that exist in both directories
+python3 scripts/compare_rvfi.py \
+    --sail-dir dii_outputs/ \
+    --rtl-dir  rtl_outputs/
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Option | Description |
+|---|---|
+| `--fields <f1,f2,...>` | Compare only these RVFI fields |
+| `--ignore <f1,f2,...>` | Skip these fields (default ignores padding) |
+| `--halt` | Include halt packets in comparison |
+| `--summary` | One pass/fail line per test, no per-packet detail |
+| `--json <file>` | Write full diff report as JSON |
+| `--max-diffs <n>` | Stop after `n` mismatches per trace (default 20) |
+
+### RVFI V1 packet fields available for comparison
+
+| Field | Width | Description |
+|---|---|---|
+| `valid` | 1 byte | 1 = valid instruction, 0 = halt |
+| `order` | 8 bytes | Monotonically increasing instruction counter |
+| `insn` | 4 bytes | 32-bit instruction encoding |
+| `trap` | 1 byte | Instruction caused a trap |
+| `halt` | 1 byte | Halt/end-of-trace marker |
+| `intr` | 1 byte | Instruction was an interrupt |
+| `rs1_addr` | 1 byte | Source register 1 index |
+| `rs2_addr` | 1 byte | Source register 2 index |
+| `rd_addr` | 1 byte | Destination register index |
+| `rs1_rdata` | 8 bytes | Value read from rs1 |
+| `rs2_rdata` | 8 bytes | Value read from rs2 |
+| `rd_wdata` | 8 bytes | Value written to rd |
+| `pc_rdata` | 8 bytes | PC before execution |
+| `pc_wdata` | 8 bytes | PC after execution (next PC) |
+| `mem_addr` | 8 bytes | Memory access address |
+| `mem_rmask` | 1 byte | Byte-enable mask for loads |
+| `mem_wmask` | 1 byte | Byte-enable mask for stores |
+| `mem_rdata` | 8 bytes | Data read from memory |
+
+### Full batch comparison workflow
+
+```bash
+# 1. Generate instruction files
+python3 gen_dii.py          # creates dii_inputs/*.txt
+
+# 2. Run Sail simulator on all files
+./scripts/batch_run.sh      # creates dii_outputs/*/rvfi.bin + run.elf
+
+# 3. Run RTL simulation (tool-specific, e.g. Verilator / Questa)
+#    RTL should write RVFI traces in the same 88-byte format to:
+#    rtl_outputs/<stem>/rvfi.bin
+
+# 4. Compare all traces
+python3 scripts/compare_rvfi.py \
+    --sail-dir dii_outputs/ \
+    --rtl-dir  rtl_outputs/ \
+    --summary \
+    --json results.json
+
+# 5. Inspect mismatches
+python3 scripts/compare_rvfi.py \
+    --sail dii_outputs/test_007/rvfi.bin \
+    --rtl  rtl_outputs/test_007/rvfi.bin
+```
+
+---
+
+## Quick-start Cheat Sheet
+
+```bash
+# ── Setup ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+eval $(opam env)
+
+# ── Checkout ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+git clone --branch dii-read-from-file --recurse-submodules \
+    https://github.com/CHERIoT-Platform/cheriot-sail.git
+cd cheriot-sail
+
+# ── Build ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+make csim                                  # standard simulator (ELF)
+make ELFIO_DIR=/usr/include rvfi           # RVFI DII simulator
+
+# ── Run ELF ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+./c_emulator/cheriot_sim path/to/program.elf
+
+# ── Run instruction file ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
+./c_emulator/cheri_riscv_rvfi_RV32 -f c_emulator/test_exc1.txt
+
+# ── Run with RVFI trace and named ELF dump ────────────────────────────────
+./c_emulator/cheri_riscv_rvfi_RV32 \
+    --instr-file  dii_inputs/test_01.txt \
+    --rvfi-output dii_outputs/test_01/rvfi.bin \
+    --elf-output  dii_outputs/test_01/run.elf
+
+# ── Batch run all instruction files ───────────────────────────────────────
+./scripts/batch_run.sh --instr-dir dii_inputs --output-dir dii_outputs
+
+# ── Compare Sail vs RTL traces ────────────────────────────────────────────
+python3 scripts/compare_rvfi.py \
+    --sail-dir dii_outputs/ --rtl-dir rtl_outputs/ --summary
+
+# ── Re-run from dump ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+./c_emulator/cheriot_sim memdump_000000.elf
+
+# ── Socket mode ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+./c_emulator/cheri_riscv_rvfi_RV32 -r 8000
+```
